vchiq: walk a kernel bulk buffer by bytes, not by ints

create_pagelist() builds the scatter list that tells VideoCore where to
DMA a bulk transfer.  For a kernel (vmalloc) buffer it walks the buffer a
page at a time:

	struct page *pg =
		vmalloc_to_page(((unsigned int *)bulk->offset +
				 (actual_pages * PAGE_SIZE)));

bulk->offset is a void *.  Casting it to unsigned int * makes the
addition scale by sizeof(unsigned int), so page N is looked up at byte
offset N * PAGE_SIZE * 4 = N * 16384 instead of N * 4096.  Page 0 is
right because 0 * anything is 0; every page after it names a page four
times too far into the buffer.

rpi-6.12.y had this right — the pointer was a char * and the arithmetic
was in bytes.  The bug arrived with the bulk_params refactor that moved
create_pagelist() from vchiq_arm.c into vchiq_core.c, and it is present
in rpi-6.16.y, rpi-6.17.y and rpi-6.18.y.

What it does to a capture: VideoCore writes the encoded frame into the
pages it was given, so the frame's first 4096 bytes land at buffer offset
0 and its second 4096 bytes land at offset 16384.  The driver then hands
userspace bytes 0..bytesused-1 of that buffer, which contain

	    0 ..  4095   frame bytes 0..4095       (correct)
	 4096 .. 16383   never written             (zeros)
	16384 .. 20479   frame bytes 4096..8191    (correct, wrong place)

Measured on 1280x720 H.264 at 30 fps, straight off /dev/video0 with the
USB gadget not involved (v4l2-ctl --stream-mmap --stream-to):

	  total bytes                       2685760
	  non-zero bytes                    1227688   (45.7%)
	  non-zero bytes per frame             4092   (~1 page)

and in the recorded stream, over 689 frames:

	  P slices with exactly 4096 live bytes    634  (92%)
	  IDR slices with exactly 20453 live bytes  11  (20480 = 16384 + 4096)
	  interior zero runs, length                     exactly 12288
	                                                 (16384 - 4096)
	  decoder errors, all "bytestream -N"      662

Every one of those numbers is what the 4x stride predicts.  The frame
lengths are correct throughout, so nothing downstream can detect this;
the transport faithfully carries a buffer that is 55% zeros.

This affects every vchiq bulk transfer from a kernel buffer larger than
one page, not just the camera.

Signed-off-by: DashBerry <dashberry@localhost>

diff --git a/drivers/staging/vc04_services/interface/vchiq_arm/vchiq_core.c b/drivers/staging/vc04_services/interface/vchiq_arm/vchiq_core.c
--- a/drivers/staging/vc04_services/interface/vchiq_arm/vchiq_core.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/vc04_services/interface/vchiq_arm/vchiq_core.c
@@ -1590,8 +1590,8 @@
 		for (actual_pages = 0; actual_pages < num_pages;
 		     actual_pages++) {
 			struct page *pg =
-				vmalloc_to_page(((unsigned int *)bulk->offset +
-						 (actual_pages * PAGE_SIZE)));
+				vmalloc_to_page(((char *)bulk->offset +
+						 (actual_pages * PAGE_SIZE)));
 			size_t bytes = PAGE_SIZE - off;

 			if (!pg) {
